# This project is on Yarn (yarn.lock is the tracked lockfile). A stray `npm install` writes
# a competing package-lock.json and resolves a different tree, which is what produced the
# "invalid or damaged lockfile" warning. Ignore it so an accidental npm run cannot be
# committed and cannot become a second source of truth. Use yarn.
package-lock.json

